21	 * Minimal local deployment entry point: validates every selected
22	 * process's configuration up front, runs the control-database migration,
23	 * builds each app, runs apps/worker once (see below), then starts and
24	 * supervises apps/api and apps/web (production `start`) as long-running
25	 * child processes.
26	 *
27	 * apps/worker currently only logs its own startup and exits (no queue
28	 * consumer exists yet — see AGENTS.md/context/stack.yml: background-job
29	 * technology is still undecided, and this task does not decide it or turn
30	 * the worker into one). It is therefore run as a completing STEP here,
31	 * like build/migrate, not as a supervised long-running service: treating
32	 * its intentional, preserved exit as a supervised process's "unexpected
33	 * exit" would tear down an otherwise-successful deployment. When a real
34	 * queue consumer is implemented, apps/worker belongs in the supervised
